  Time [ ] / Pause Space / Save F5 / Load F9 / Quit dialog Escape

  @{"Flight details" link flight}
  @{"Navigation    " link navigation}
  @{"Contents      " link main}

  @{b}Sound and expanded controllers@{ub}
  Put your own ProTracker MODs in the music drawer beside the executable:
  battle, planetary-flight, space-flight, docked and game-over subdrawers.
  Names can be tune.mod or MOD.tune (case insensitive). No music is supplied.
  Tracks change randomly at song end and on situation changes, excluding the
  previous selection when alternatives exist. Empty subdrawers stay silent;
  engine, laser, damage, explosion, docking and jump effects still play.
  Battle takes priority for a living hostile within 12 km. Planetary music
  plays below 12 km above terrain. Landing/docking and death have own folders.
  Menus retain the current situation; pause mutes and holds music.
  --nosound disables all audio. Time compression does not speed up music.

  MODs preload into RAM before ECS/AGA takeover: at most 128 tracks, 4 MiB per
  file and 16 MiB total, subject to free memory. Invalid files are skipped.
  See music/README.txt for supported formats and limits. Add files before
  launch. Saves retain preloaded music. Native Paula uses 256 ms buffers;
  slow frames can repeat a block. RTG uses queued audio.device playback.
  Real-hardware playback/performance remains to be checked.

  CD32 (lowlevel.library V40+): red fire, blue brake, yellow radar contact,
  green autopilot, forward/reverse thrust and Play pause.
  --analog selects a physical POT-counter joystick in port 2. Keep it
  centred at startup; press C to recalibrate. Physical devices need QA.

  @{b}Release and timing@{ub}
  CPU builds: Astralbound.000 (68000), Astralbound.020/.030 (no FPU; also LC040/LC060),
  Astralbound.020fpu (68020/030 + 68881/68882), Astralbound.040 and Astralbound.060 (full
  CPU with FPU). The FPU builds are faster at rendering on those machines.
  --rtg16 opens high-colour output through the CGX/P96 driver. The renderer
  still uses its original indexed scene palette. --rtg retains 8-bit output.
  --profile exits after 120 frames and reports render/output timings.
  Astralbound-benchmark.<cpu> measures scene rendering and C2P into Chip RAM.

  Open Install with SYS:Utilities/Installer V42.12+ and choose a drawer.
  Existing astralbound.sav is preserved. CPU icons accept MODE=ECS/AGA/RTG/RTG16
  and LOWRES, NOSOUND, ANALOG tooltypes. Play-AGA/Play-RTG/Play-RTG16 scripts
  use Astralbound.020; Play-ECS-Lowres uses Astralbound.000.
  The original boot ADF starts ECS 320 x 200 with a user-supplied OS3 ROM.
  Tested with 2 MiB Chip and 8 MiB Fast; unexpanded A500s are not validated.
  Escape returns to the boot CLI. A writable ADF can hold a commander save.

@endnode
